# Line endings.
#
# A shell script with CRLF line endings fails on macOS and Linux, because the kernel reads
# the shebang line as "/bin/sh\r". Shell scripts and JavaScript must keep LF.
#
# Text is normalised to LF in the repository. On checkout, Git uses the platform default
# for files that are not listed here, so a Windows editor still sees its own line endings
# for Markdown.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF in the working tree, and must keep their executable bit.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.ps1         text eol=crlf

# Source and data files.
*.js          text eol=lf
*.mjs         text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.gitignore   text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary files, if any are added later.
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.ico         binary
